<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT- Bancomer downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT- Bancomer downgraded.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santander Investment said Friday that  it had downgraded the B shares and ADRs of Mexican bank, Grupo Financiero  Bancomer, to market perform from a buy.</p>
<p>-- Santander expects earnings per ADR of $1.07, $1.26 and $1.80 for  1997, 1998, and 1999, respectively.</p>
<p>Bancomer reported a 1996 loss per ADR of $1.67, Santander said in  a statement.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We believe that the expected improvements going forward have already  been discounted by the market and that further increases in share  price are unlikely to rival those of the IPC,&quot; said analysts Robert  Lacoursiere and Patrick Boucher.</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
